 "summary": "The apply now honours the fate. The engine installs the org-scoping service's platformGlobalObjects first thing in ObjectQLPlugin.start(). A host that brings its own ObjectQLPlugin (a lazy wrapper under the framework's plugin name) replaces the CLI's engine, the declaration boot suppresses that engine's start(), and measureComposedCoverage, which stands in for that start(), only repeated the registry-to-driver binding. So the declared object was planned with organization_id, the differ proposed no drop, and column-drops answered not-proposed. measureComposedCoverage now installs the declaration first, through core's readDeploymentOrgScopingEntitlement and the registry's own setDeploymentPlatformGlobalObjects. There is no new export and nothing outside packages/cli. Pinned through the real command on SQLite (red before the fix, two controls unchanged), with an ablation leg.",
 "h1_cause": "(c), the engine's start() is suppressed in the host-owned-engine shape, and the CLI's stand-in pass skipped the declaration install. Measured on the apply boot (bootSchemaStack with composeHostStack + composeServedPlatform + composeAuthGatedSecurity, DDL deferred) over a v17 SQLite copy, before the fix. Shape A (provider in config.plugins, CLI's own engine): org-scoping present with platformGlobalObjects [sys_osgc_ledger]; the registry plans no organization_id (systemFields.tenant false); the drift proposes unmapped_column drop_column. Shape B (same provider, host's own lazy ObjectQLPlugin, the control-plane shape schema-migrate.host-composition.integration.test.ts reproduces): org-scoping present with the declaration, but the registry plans organization_id and the drift is empty. Shape C (OS_TENANCY_POSTURE=isolated, provider only as a host-resolved @objectstack/organizations, the way serve mounts it): org-scoping ABSENT. (a) is refuted: composeServedPlatform composes no organizations runtime (auth family = identity objects, SecurityPlugin, AuditPlugin; CAPABILITY_PROVIDERS has no organizations row). (b) is refuted for the config shape: the host provider's init() runs on the declaration boot and registers org-scoping (A and B). After the fix, B reads like A (no organization_id, drop_column proposed), A is unchanged and gets no new note, and C is unchanged (reported, not fixed).",
 "before_after": {
