 "deviations": [
  "/verify (the objectui metadata-admin designer-preview browser check) not run before commit: the diff touches no objectui or designer surface.",
  "Rig: the org-scoping provider is a structural plugin, not an OrganizationsPlugin subclass. It registers org-scoping in init() with platformGlobalObjects and providesServices, as OrganizationsPlugin does. @objectstack/organizations is not an @objectstack/cli dependency, and adding it would move package.json and the lockfile.",
  "Rig extends Zone 3's shape with the host's own lazy ObjectQLPlugin. Measured: without it (shape A) the declaration was already honoured before the fix, so only the engine shape gives the red pin.",
  "origin/main 8d1fb1fb2 was merged in before the PR (merge commit 06761db20, rest/runtime only, both rebuilt). It carries git's default message and no trailer pair. origin/main later moved to 09dd53719; not merged again (no conflict, PR open).",
  "Commit 6088127b0 carries the model-free trailer pair (AGENTS.md and the dispatch), not the harness reminder's model-named Co-Authored-By."
 ],
 "open_questions": [
  {
   "question": "Which shape does cloud's control plane use to compose its org-scoping provider? This PR honours a provider in config.plugins, with or without the host's own engine. A provider that arrives only through serve's walled-posture organizations mount (shape C) is still not seen by the migration boot.",
   "options": [
    "A: the cloud seat reruns the objectstack-ai/cloud#2709 round-7 --apply measurement on this head before the card is accepted (no code here)",
    "B: also mirror serve's walled-posture organizations mount in composeServedPlatform now. That needs either a second copy of serve's inline rule, or moving the rule to a shared reader (a serve.ts refactor outside this card's surface)."
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. Business need: this repo's records (the host-owned-engine fixture header in schema-migrate.host-composition.integration.test.ts, the coverage docblock in schema-migration-plugins.ts, membership-policy-gate.ts on the control-plane preset constructing AuthPlugin) describe cloud's preset composing its own engine and auth family in config.plugins, which is shape B, covered here. Long term: B adds a second copy of serve's rule. AI safety: unchanged, since no producer of shape C is named. Scope: B grows the change for zero measured pull."
  },
  {
   "question": "os migrate apply --allow-destructive drops a host-declared platform-global object's organization_id ahead of the ceremony (measured; the drop gate knows only the platform inventory). This PR extends that from hosts on the CLI's own engine to hosts that bring their own. Land this first, or hold it until the gate is widened?",
   "options": [
    "A: land this PR; the seat files the gate finding (class b, measured) as its own card",
    "B: hold this PR until the gate refuses every organization_id drop ahead of the ceremony's verified marker"
   ],
   "recommendation": "A. The gap already exists for every host on the CLI's own engine. The drop needs the explicit --allow-destructive flag and is listed in the plan before it applies. Widening the gate from the platform inventory to any organization_id is a gate-scope decision for its own card. The ceremony's column-drop path, which this card owes, gets no safer by waiting."
  }
 ],
 "out_of_scope_findings": [
  "class: b · reach: public door measured. On this PR's fixture at 06761db20, os migrate apply --database-url file:v17.db --allow-destructive --yes --json exited 0 and applied drop_column organization_id on sys_osgc_ledger and sys_osgc_held, two host-declared platform-global objects, with no organization-ownership marker on the database · evidence: organization-ownership-drop-gate.ts builds CEREMONY_TABLES from ORGANIZATION_OWNERSHIP_INVENTORY only. Its header contract says 'the drop of organization_id on any table in the ceremony's inventory waits for the ceremony's verified marker', and ADR-0131 D10 puts 'cloud's supplement for cloud-declared ones' in that inventory. Seam: spec:OrganizationOwnershipSupplementSchema → runtime:packages/cli/src/commands/migrate/apply.ts ceremonyOrganizationColumnDrops. Pre-existing for a host on the CLI's own engine (that shape's drift proposed the drop before this PR); this PR extends it to the host-owned-engine shape · dedupe words: 'allow-destructive organization_id host supplement', 'ceremonyOrganizationColumnDrops inventory', 'drop gate host-declared platform-global', 'organization-ownership-drop-gate CEREMONY_TABLES'",
  "carrier: none · noted, not filed (PR Acceptance notes). Shape C: composeServedPlatform does not mirror serve's walled-posture organizations mount (Serve.ORGANIZATIONS_RUNTIME_PKG through importFromHost). So a host whose org-scoping provider arrives only that way has no org-scoping on any composeHostStack boot. Measured on the apply boot with OS_TENANCY_POSTURE=isolated and a fixture host package: org-scoping absent, declared object planned with organization_id, before and after this PR. No pull from open code: the open OrganizationsPlugin declares no platformGlobalObjects, and no producer is named."
 ]
